plan/post-release/features/spec-pppoe-vpp-dataplane.md, AC-27, requires:
"Readiness and counter publication are refused. Process retirement requires the
exact retained physical process proof; a claimed PID, logical generation or
another child's completed wait cannot retire a live foreign peer."

LL-FD-RECEIVE-DEADLINE in docs/architecture/linux-limitations.md records the
shared-library constraint. Deadline-aware descriptor receipt is a prerequisite
to completing that ownership check. The unpatched fd.go in the pinned upstream
module has SHA256 07e3fc99b7f6934c78e30e2ced97b7e55ebe7d906aefa5730cbf169e768d9e86.

Receive through the original UnixConn's poller,
so its read deadline applies and the original receive completes on timeout.
Keep Get's public API, nil payload, control-buffer size, filenames and returned
file ownership. Parse only the ancillary bytes received. The caller still
closes every returned file, including a partial result with a parsing error.
If ReadMsgUnix reports EOF with ancillary data from a zero-payload packet,
parse that data normally. Closed-peer EOF remains the receive error. A
completed message without ancillary data returns io.ErrUnexpectedEOF.
These refusals replace the former incidental padding-parse EINVAL, without
returning files or changing their ownership. Other receive errors stay errors.
Put and the existing control-truncation policy are unchanged.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a
vendored module". Deliver through ./le setup install and commit its vendor
result. Delete when the upstream module honors the same receive contract.

